00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:32.320
Now here is something most retail investors get wrong with tax loss harvesting. Imagine you bought

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:41.200
XIU last month at $38.50 and it now trades at $36.80 after the broader market dip.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:48.740
Selling locks in a $1.70 per unit capital loss that can offset gains elsewhere in your

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:57.220
TFSA or RRSP. The superficial loss rule blocks you from repurchasing the identical ETF for 30 days.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:04.460
The pro move is swapping into a near identical but distinct product such as XIC for that window before

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:13.200
switching back. The 2024 inclusion rate increase to 50 percent on gains above $250,000 makes harvesting

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:19.560
losses even more valuable. Every dollar of loss now saves 25 cents in tax instead of 20.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:26.580
Losses carry forward indefinitely and can be applied against future gains or even up to $3,000 of

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:34.120
ordinary income per year. The T50008 slip your broker issues in February reports proceeds but not

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:42.560
your adjusted cost base. Track ACB yourself or use software to avoid CRA disputes. The biggest mistake

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.780
is selling and immediately buying the same ticker. Always map a 30 day substitute pair in advance

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:55.400
using your brokerage's ETF comparison tool. Before we wrap, tomorrow I will check whether oil

